    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0787" n="1621" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 654.119/242</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-09T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 11, 1.45 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3313. For War Trade Board [from Dresel]:</p>
                <p>No. 27. My No. 16, April 28.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d662-f1"/> New cotton agreement
                    was signed May 8 without change from terms stated. Letter stating no American
                    cotton will be exported any form to Central Powers will be delivered
                    immediately. Dresel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d662-f1" n="2" xml:id="d662-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the principal terms of the cotton agreement as signed are given in
                    the Minister’s telegram No. 2929, Mar. 24, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg1605">p. 1605</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
